hey what's up my name's Samuel Leeds I'm  a property investor and I have  personally been involved in over 300  property deals over the last 10 years  and in this video I want to talk about  property deal sourcing what does it mean  to be a deal sorcerer and you may hear a  lot of people talking about deals  sourcing or property flipping packaging  deals like what does it mean exactly  what are the different expressions mean  and should you be a deal sorcerer so  first let me say this if you hear people  talking about flipping properties on a  property flipper that is very different  from a property sorcerer a property  sorcerer a property packager or deal  packager it doesn't deal seller that all  means the same things a property flipper  is someone who finds a property deal  they buy it they do it up and then they  pass it on to someone else so they flip  it on to someone else that's a property  flipper a property sorcerer and you may  also have heard people call them  describe themselves as a trader by trade  deals I'm a deal trader I'm a deal  package a deal saw sodor seller that all  means the same thing I don't know why  there's so many different expressions  for it but what that is is that is when  you find a deal you don't buy it you  don't own it  you just find it you negotiate it at a  set price and then you pass it on to an  investor for a fee effectively you're  like a broker in the middle now the  great thing about being a deal saw so  I'm gonna talk about what the good  things the bad things hopefully you kind  of get what it is now  so you find an opportunity you find a  deal negotiate the price pass it on to  an investor take your fee never own it  the great thing about it is there's no  risk or there's very very little risk  because when you buy a house what are  the risks well the risk is that you  can't rent it out the risk is that it  goes down in value the risk is that the  tenants trashed the property there are  risks whereas when you are packaging a  property and passing on to somebody else  the only risk you have is the risk of  having a bad reputation or a bad  conscience of passing on a bad property  but financially speaking  you have zero risks you have no risks  financially because you don't ever own  the house you'll just finding it and  passing it on to somebody else so that's  the first pro the second Pro is it can  be a very very Luke  TIF and I mean very lucrative I I've  sold hundreds of these deals on average  if you find a beer and you pass it on to  an investor they'll pay you between two  and five thousand pounds now you might  think why would someone pay you  thousands of pounds to go and find a  property and the reason is is because  the probably the most expensive thing  that you're ever gonna buy is a house  generally speaking if I say to someone  what's the most expensive thing you've  ever bought it's a house maybe followed  by a wedding maybe a car and then  generally you might buy small things  every day like food go out for dinners  now if you are paying someone to find  you a nice dinner where's a good place  to go and eat oh it's probably this  place you might pay some tip somebody a  couple of pound a few pounds because  you're only spending 50 pounds on the  dinner but when you're spending 50  thousand pounds on an investment or  maybe five hundred thousand pounds  something so big something so expensive  it's a property investment do you think  that you've been prepared to pay  somebody a couple thousand pounds to not  only find you a good deal but also to  negotiate the price down if someone's  negotiated a property from 100,000 to  80,000 they've knocked off 20,000 pounds  would you pay them two thousand pounds  to do that and the answer is of course  so as a deal sorcerer if you're out  looking for properties and you're  knocking down the prices and you're  negotiating good deals you are paid  handsomely to do that so there's no risk  the second thing it is very very  lucrative the third great thing about  deal sourcing is you are getting paid to  scalp the market for good property  investments and what's going to happen  if you're a deal sorcerer is you're  going to come across such good property  investments some of them are gonna be so  good and you're gonna get them so cheap  and they're gonna be such great  investments that it's going to pain you  to sell them for a measly two grand  you're gonna be like man I've found this  house it's it's 200 grand but I've got  it down to 150 and all  so when I buy it I'm gonna be able to  get some planning permission and push  the value up and I'm gonna rent it out  and such a good deal I want five grand  and you'll sell it for five grand and  then another one will come along just as  good even better and you're like I don't  even wanna let this go for five grand  and what you'll do is you'll think  actually know what I want this myself  and you'll find a way of financing it  yourself you'll probably use your  property investors that you've built up  as a deal sorcerer and you'll get them  to fund it but you're going to end up  being a property investor as a deal  sorcerer not just a property investor  but the kind of property investor that  gets the absolute creme of the creme  deals so that's the great things about  being a deal sorcerer they're not so  great things about being a deal sorcerer  are firstly it comes with a lot of  responsibility because if you're passing  deals on to investors and they're  trusting you and taking your word for it  and paying you thousands of pounds  because of a lot of responsibility so I  highly recommend a couple things firstly  get educated and get good make sure that  you're only finding good deals and  secondly make sure that you have proper  terms and conditions with your investors  so that they know that you've found the  property you've negotiated it but it  doesn't mean that you're responsible  forever and ever that this property is  going to be a good investment they have  to do their own research their own due  diligence and you're gonna have to make  that really clear in the terms and  conditions so that's the first con the  second con is you don't actually as a  deal sorcerer unless you systemize it  and start employing people which is  possible it doesn't give you passive  income so if you buy a property and you  rent it out it's going to keep giving  you rent every single month whereas  there's a deal sorcerer you have to keep  working keep working keep working to  getting paid some of my students tell me  Samuel it's not passive income but it is  massive income and I can use the profits  to invest into property that's going to  give me a passive income and there's a  really good argument in that but my  experience as a deal sorcerer and as a  property investor says that deal  sourcing does come with a lot of work it  does come with a lot of headaches you've  got investors calling you it's not  something that you can do you know one  hour a week this is gonna be something  you're going to really have to dedicate  your time to however if you could do one  deal a week  that's gonna give you about 10,000  pounds a month and I've got many many  students that are doing that and more so  it is lucrative part of the con is it's  gonna come with some hard work the last  con of Deal sourcing is there are a lot  of people that call themselves deal  sources that have never sold a deal and  they spam Facebook groups and they hound  estate agents and they do it all wrong  so with some people with some  professionals deal sources I've got a  little bit of a bad rep and people think  oh there's so many deal sources but let  me tell you this I know there's a lot of  people that call themself deal sources  but actually people doing it properly  that I've learned how to do it  step-by-step and good deal sources  there's not that many so if you learn  how to find good deals how do it network  with investors and you learn how to do  it properly you will be able to sell  deals very very quickly and make a lot  of money doing it so if you want to  learn more about deals selling or deal  packaging whatever you want to call it  as a strategy my advice would be I do  regularly run training webinars advanced  training webinars for free where I teach  you more about deal sourcing so if you  want to register so that you're the  first to know and I'm gonna be running  one of these live webinars then in the  description box below you can just put  your details in and I'll keep you posted  on any future training that I'm running  also if you want to learn more about  deal sourcing right now I have done  videos on YouTube before you can check  those out right there also don't forget  to subscribe to the channel you can  subscribe right there subscribe  turn the notification bell on smash a  like drop a comment thank you so much  for watching I'll see you next time

